/*!
\mainpage Virtual Experimentation Framework User Manual

This manual describes how to use the Virtual Experimentation Framework and 
how to interpret the results obtained from the VEF.
The manual includes:
- \ref page_gettingstarted describing the installation of the VEF software.
- \ref user_reference that presents main components of the VEF and discusses 
  how to operate it. 
  The User Reference covers:
  - \ref page_expert_mode that provides a complete control over all the knobs  in the VEF software, 
  - \ref page_simple_mode that helps to carry out standard tasks with minimal
    effort, while sticking to pre-defined defaults, and
  - \ref page_utilities that facilitate a more integral use of the VEF.
- \ref guided_tour that gives a step-by-step overview of typical use cases where the VEF is applied.
- \ref theory that introduces the foundations of the VEF software and crystal
  plasticity models it utilizes.
- \ref examples that summarizes the collection of sample problems bundled with the VEF.
*/


